---
// /manifesto — the ethos, stated plainly and quotably. Built to be lifted: short,
// declarative lines and blockquotes that read well as a pull-quote in an AI answer
// or a featured snippet. Speakable JSON-LD points voice assistants at the lede and
// the quotes.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': 'https://blaksyd.com/manifesto/#webpage',
    url: 'https://blaksyd.com/manifesto/',
    name: 'The Blaksyd Manifesto',
    description:
      'The Blaksyd manifesto: most apps want your attention; Blaksyd wants your life to be better. No engagement-bait, no manufactured FOMO, no dependency-by-design.',
    isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://blaksyd.com/#website' },
    about: { '@id': 'https://blaksyd.com/#organization' },
    breadcrumb: { '@id': 'https://blaksyd.com/manifesto/#breadcrumb' },
    primaryImageOfPage: {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      url: 'https://blaksyd.com/assets/blaksyd-manifesto.png',
      caption: 'Most apps want your attention. Blaksyd wants your life to be better.',
    },
    speakable: {
      '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification',
      cssSelector: ['.pg-lede', '.prose blockquote'],
    },
  },
];
---

<Page
  title="The Blaksyd Manifesto — attention is not the goal"
  description="Most apps want your attention. Blaksyd wants your life to be better. No engagement-bait, no manufactured FOMO, no dependency-by-design — safety first, resonance over vanity metrics."
  image="/assets/blaksyd-manifesto.png"
  kicker="Manifesto"
  kickerClass="k-gold"
  heading="Most apps want your attention."
  accent="We want your life to be better."
  lede="Blaksyd is built on a refusal: that technology shaped around you should make your life better, not just longer on a screen. This is what we stand for."
  heroImage="/assets/blaksyd-manifesto.png"
  heroAlt="The Blaksyd manifesto — most apps want your attention, Blaksyd wants your life to be better."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Manifesto', href: '/manifesto/' }]}
  schema={schema}
>
  <section>
    <blockquote>Most apps want your attention. Blaksyd wants your life to be better.</blockquote>
    <p>
      That single line is the test every feature has to pass. If it’s built to capture you, it doesn’t belong
      here. If it’s built to serve you, it does.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we refuse</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>No engagement-bait.</b> We don’t design to maximise time-on-screen.</li>
      <li><b>No manufactured FOMO.</b> We don’t invent urgency to keep you anxious and scrolling.</li>
      <li><b>No dependency-by-design.</b> We don’t build hooks meant to make you need us.</li>
      <li><b>No vanity metrics.</b> Hollow likes measure nothing real, so we don’t keep score that way.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we stand for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>You at the centre.</b> Every feature, interaction, and conversation revolves around who you are and what you need right now.</li>
      <li><b>Human + AI, together.</b> <a href="/blak/">Blak</a> and <a href="/persona/">Persona</a> to know you; <a href="/minit/">Minit</a> and <a href="/nexus/">Nexus</a> to bring real people close.</li>
      <li><b>Safety first — on both sides.</b> Protections for the people who reach out <em>and</em> the people who show up to listen. We don’t operate under “the user is always right.”</li>
      <li><b>Resonance over reach.</b> We recognise the real impact of what you share, not how loud it is.</li>
      <li><b>Your world stays yours.</b> Anonymous by default, you control what is remembered, and we don’t sell your personal data.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <blockquote>The better future isn’t coming — it’s yours to enter.</blockquote>
    <p>Blaksyd is pre-launch, with an open waitlist. <a href="/about/">Learn how it works →</a></p>
  </section>
</Page>
